# hermetic-probe-keep — the value sweep's allowed sites, one per line:
# <file><TAB><allowed text>. A row allows exactly its text at its file:
# the sweep blanks every allowed text out of a hit line and the line must
# then match no class pattern and no token — a second value beside an
# allowed one is still a hit, and nothing is allowed by file alone. A
# row's text therefore covers the whole value it allows (the URL, not the
# port in it), and the sweep holds it to that: a name character touching
# the text — a letter, digit, `_` or `/` on either side, `.` before it, `-`
# or a URL's `?`, `#`, `&`, `=` or `@` after it — means the value runs on,
# and the longer value is the hit.
# The sweep leaves this file out of its corpus and no other.
#
# The marketplace's own addresses, the node's and ymer's — public by role
